Now insert the language switcher + hero video sections after the mobile menu block (line ~292 originally, now shifted). Use the marker `/* ---------- Reveal on scroll ---------- */`.

Language code:
```
  /* ---------- Language switcher (interface language) ---------- */
  var langSwitch = $("[data-lang-switch]");
  var langToggle = $("[data-lang-toggle]");
  var langOptions = $$(".lang-option");

  function closeLangMenu() {...}
  function applyLanguage(code) {
    var dict = UI_TEXT[code] || UI_TEXT.ar;
    currentLang = UI_TEXT[code] ? code : "ar";
    document.documentElement.lang = currentLang;
    $$("[data-i18n]").forEach(...)
    ...
    var current = $("[data-lang-current]"); current.textContent = LANG_LABELS[currentLang] || ...
    langOptions.forEach...
    updateClock();
    writeStore(STORE.lang, currentLang);
  }
```
Important: Should not overwrite `data-i18n` text if dict missing. Use `var value = dict[key]; if (value != null) node.textContent = value;`.
For placeholder: `node.setAttribute("placeholder", value)`.
For aria: `node.setAttribute("aria-label", value)`.

The language button label update. The button's native label should display the current language in its own script. Use `dir="auto"`.

Apply at init: `applyLanguage(currentLang)` — but this writes storage and runs before reveal; fine. It also calls updateClock (defined). Good.

Potential issue: `data-i18n` on the footer `<a>` policy links — setting textContent is fine.

Toggle behavior:
```
if (langSwitch && langToggle) {
  langToggle.addEventListener("click", function(event){ event.preventDefault(); var open=...; ... });
  langSwitch.addEventListener("keydown", function(event){ if (event.key==="Escape" && is-open) { close; langToggle.focus(); } });
  langOptions.forEach(function(option){ option.addEventListener("click", function(){ applyLanguage(option.getAttribute("data-lang")); closeLangMenu(); langToggle.focus(); }); });
  document.addEventListener("click", function(event){ if (!langSwitch.classList.contains("is-open")) return; if (event.target.closest("[data-lang-switch]")) return; closeLangMenu(); });
}
```
When opening, also close nav dropdowns. `closeAllDropdowns()` is defined earlier in scope (function). Call it.

Ensure the nav dropdown click outside handler doesn't close lang (it only affects nav). Fine.

Hero video:
```
var heroVideo = $("[data-hero-video]");
if (heroVideo && !reduceMotion) {
  var playlist = (heroVideo.getAttribute("data-playlist") || "").split("|").filter(Boolean);
  var clipIndex = 0;
  function showVideo() { heroVideo.classList.add("is-ready"); }
  heroVideo.addEventListener("loadeddata", showVideo, { once: true });
  if (heroVideo.readyState >= 2) showVideo();
  heroVideo.addEventListener("error", function(){ heroVideo.classList.remove("is-ready"); });
  if (playlist.length > 1) {
    heroVideo.removeAttribute("loop");
    heroVideo.addEventListener("ended", function () {
      clipIndex = (clipIndex + 1) % playlist.length;
      heroVideo.src = playlist[clipIndex];
      heroVideo.load();
      var play = heroVideo.play();
      if (play && play.catch) play.catch(function(){});
    });
  } else if (playlist.length === 1) {
    heroVideo.setAttribute("loop", "");
  }
  var playPromise = heroVideo.play();
  if (playPromise && playPromise.catch) playPromise.catch(function(){});
} else if (heroVideo) {
  heroVideo.removeAttribute("autoplay");
  heroVideo.pause();
  heroVideo.style.display = "none";
}
```
Note `reduceMotion` was computed at load. Good.

Add `heroVideo.removeAttribute("loop")` only when >1; markup has no loop already.

One concern: changing `src` attribute after a `<source>` child exists — the source child will take precedence on load? If you set `video.src`, it overrides source elements? Per spec, setting src attribute should override child sources. To be safe, remove `<source>` on ended or create source only initially. Better markup: use `src` on the `<video>` instead of `<source>` child. Let me change markup to `<video ... src="...">` (no source). Then swapping `src` works reliably. Edit build.js.

Also `preload="metadata"` + autoplay is fine.

