Opacity stays 0 and visibility hidden even after class is-open because CSS transition frozen in background tab (same issue as hero video). So can't measure the visible state transitions. But the rect with right 373 confirms geometry overflows at 320. `body` overflow-x hidden clips it, so part of language menu will be cut off. Need fix.

Why is menu anchored at left 81? Because RTL `inset-inline-end:0` = left. The header actions are left side; the switch at ~81. The menu should extend to the left toward viewport edge? There's only 81px space. So we need at mobile to anchor right edge to switch's right edge and extend left (but then left = 119-292 = -173, also offscreen).

Better: position fixed-like full-width sheet under the header on small screens: `position: fixed; left: 14px; right: 14px; width: auto; top: calc(var(--header-h) + 8px);` This avoids overflow entirely. At ≤560 or ≤720, use fixed full width. But in iframe, position fixed relative to iframe viewport (good). Since header height 84/94, top = header + 8. But the header isn't sticky? `.site-header` maybe sticky. Let's check. If header sticky, fixed menu under it. On mobile, menu width 100vw - 28 and inset 14. Good.

Alternatively use `inset-inline-end: auto; inset-inline-start: 0`? Not enough.

Implement at max-width: 720px:
```
.lang-switch__menu {
  position: fixed;
  top: calc(var(--header-h) + 6px);
  left: 12px;
  right: 12px;
  width: auto;
  max-width: none;
  max-height: calc(100vh - var(--header-h) - 24px);
  inset-inline: 12px;
}
```
`inset-inline` sets both start and end; but position fixed containing block viewport. Need override `inset-inline-end: 0` and set left/right. CSS logical vs physical: use `inset-inline: 12px; inset-block-start: calc(...)` and `inset-block-end: auto;` But `top` also set earlier; override `top: calc(...)`. Simpler physical: `position: fixed; top: calc(var(--header-h) + 8px); left: 12px; right: 12px; width: auto; inset-inline-end: auto;`. Since site is RTL but physical left/right fine.

But the header might be inside a container with transform? Fixed positions to viewport. Header height variable 84/94. At ≤560 84, 561-720 94. Good.

At 320, top=92, width=296, right=308. Fits. But menu grid 2 columns with labels; okay. Height up to 100vh - 108. At 320x900 fine.

Alternatively, for 400-720 the current menu fits except 320 (right 373 > 320) and 360 (413 > 360) and 400 (423 > 400). So mobile fixed sheet is best for <=560.

Use breakpoint ≤560 (already styles exist). At 560 menu right 423 < 560 fine, but full width is nicer. Could apply only ≤420:
At 320: available left of switch? No.
At 360: overflow 53.
At 400: overflow 23.
At 414: 423 > 414 overflow 9.
At 560 fits.

Use ≤560 to be safe and consistent. Implement:
```
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .lang-switch__menu {
    position: fixed;
    top: calc(var(--header-h) + 8px);
    left: 12px;
    right: 12px;
    width: auto;
    max-width: none;
    max-height: calc(100vh - var(--header-h) - 28px);
    inset-inline: auto 12px; /* wait logical overrides physical? */
  }
}
```
Careful: original `.lang-switch__menu` sets `inset-inline-end: 0`. Physical `right: 12px` and logical `inset-inline-end: 12px` conflict; in RTL, inset-inline-end is left. To avoid confusion, override with logical:
```
inset-inline: 12px; /* start and end both 12px => left/right 12 in RTL */
inset-block-start: calc(var(--header-h) + 8px);
inset-block-end: auto;
width: auto;
```
`top` originally set, and `inset-block-start` maps to top. Good. Set `top: auto`? Use `inset-block-start`.

Actually `inset-inline: 12px` sets both inline-start and inline-end. In RTL, start=right, end=left, so both 12. Perfect.

Set `max-height: calc(100dvh - var(--header-h) - 28px)`.

Also the `.lang-switch__menu` z-index 140; header z-index maybe 100; fine.

Let's add this CSS in the appended section near the 560 media query.

Before that, maybe improve the desktop alignment: the menu `inset-inline-end: 0` aligns with the switch's left edge, extending right. At desktop switch l=328, menu r=670 < 1440, fine. At 1101 switch l=235, r=577 < 1101. Fine. So only mobile.

